.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt PROTOC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm protoc
.Nd Protocol Buffers compiler
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /usr/libexec/protoc
.Op Fl I Ns Ar path | Fl -proto_path Ns = Ns Ar path
.Op Fl -cpp_out Ns = Ns Ar dir
.Op Fl - Ns Ar name Ns _out Ns = Ns Ar dir
.Op Fl -plugin Ns = Ns Ar protoc-gen-name Ns = Ns Ar program
.Op Fl o Ar file | Fl -descriptor_set_out Ns = Ns Ar file
.Op Fl -include_imports
.Op Fl -decode Ns = Ns Ar message_type
.Op Fl -decode_raw
.Op Fl -encode Ns = Ns Ar message_type
.Op Ar options
.Ar file.proto ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
parses Protocol Buffers definitions
.Pq Pa .proto
files and generates code for them, or converts messages between the binary
wire format and the text format.
It is installed as
.Pa /usr/libexec/protoc ,
outside the default
.Ev PATH :
base system components run it by that path, normally through the build
fragment
.Pa lib/protobuf/protoc-gen.mk ,
and it does not take the place of a Protocol Buffers compiler installed
from ports.
The base system
.Nm
contains the C++ generator.
Other generators are separate programs, called plugins, that
.Nm
runs as
.Pa protoc-gen- Ns Ar name
for an
.Fl - Ns Ar name Ns _out
option, found on
.Ev PATH
or named with
.Fl -plugin .
The base system installs three plugins for C code that uses the upb
runtime:
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/libexec/protoc-gen-upb_minitable"
.It Pa /usr/libexec/protoc-gen-upb
generates the upb C API,
.Ar name Ns Pa .upb.h .
.It Pa /usr/libexec/protoc-gen-upb_minitable
generates the upb mini-tables,
.Ar name Ns Pa .upb_minitable.c
and
.Ar name Ns Pa .upb_minitable.h .
.It Pa /usr/libexec/protoc-gen-upbdefs
generates the reflection definitions for
.Vt upb_DefPool ,
.Ar name Ns Pa .upbdefs.c
and
.Ar name Ns Pa .upbdefs.h .
.El
.Pp
The well-known types
.Pq Pa google/protobuf/*.proto
are installed in
.Pa /usr/include/private
and are found without an
.Fl I
option.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl I Ns Ar path , Fl -proto_path Ns = Ns Ar path
Search
.Ar path
for imports and input files.
May be given more than once; directories are searched in order.
.It Fl -cpp_out Ns = Ns Ar dir
Generate C++ header and source files
.Pq Ar name Ns Pa .pb.h , Ar name Ns Pa .pb.cc
in
.Ar dir .
.It Fl - Ns Ar name Ns _out Ns = Ns Ar dir
Run the plugin
.Pa protoc-gen- Ns Ar name
and write its output in
.Ar dir .
.It Fl - Ns Ar name Ns _opt Ns = Ns Ar option
Pass
.Ar option
to the generator or plugin
.Ar name .
.It Fl -plugin Ns = Ns Ar protoc-gen-name Ns = Ns Ar program
Use
.Ar program
as the plugin
.Ar protoc-gen-name .
.It Fl o Ar file , Fl -descriptor_set_out Ns = Ns Ar file
Write a
.Vt FileDescriptorSet
of the inputs to
.Ar file .
.It Fl -include_imports
With
.Fl o ,
include the imports of the inputs in the set.
.It Fl -decode Ns = Ns Ar message_type
Read a binary message of type
.Ar message_type ,
defined in the given
.Pa .proto
files, from standard input and write it in text format to standard output.
.It Fl -decode_raw
Read an arbitrary binary message from standard input and write its tag/value
pairs in text format to standard output.
No
.Pa .proto
files are needed.
.It Fl -encode Ns = Ns Ar message_type
Read a text format message of type
.Ar message_type
from standard input and write it in binary to standard output.
.It Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print all options and exit.
.El
.Pp
Arguments may also be read from a file named
.Li @ Ns Ar file ,
one per line.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/include/private/google/protobuf" -compact
.It Pa /usr/libexec/protoc
the compiler
.It Pa /usr/include/private/google/protobuf
well-known type definitions and the C++ runtime headers
.It Pa /usr/libexec/protoc-gen-upb
upb C API plugin
.It Pa /usr/libexec/protoc-gen-upb_minitable
upb mini-table plugin
.It Pa /usr/libexec/protoc-gen-upbdefs
upb reflection plugin
.It Pa /usr/share/licenses/protobuf
licence of the protobuf sources
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate C++ code for
.Pa example.proto
in the current directory:
.Pp
.Dl $ /usr/libexec/protoc --cpp_out=. example.proto
.Pp
Generate upb C code:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ /usr/libexec/protoc \e
    --plugin=protoc-gen-upb=/usr/libexec/protoc-gen-upb \e
    --plugin=protoc-gen-upb_minitable=/usr/libexec/protoc-gen-upb_minitable \e
    --upb_out=. --upb_minitable_out=. example.proto
.Ed
.Pp
Show the fields of an unknown binary message:
.Pp
.Dl $ /usr/libexec/protoc --decode_raw < message.bin
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libotelexport 3
.Pp
.Lk https://protobuf.dev/ "Protocol Buffers documentation"
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
29.6 first appeared in the 5BSD base system, with the C++ runtime as the
private libraries
.Pa libprivateprotobuf
and
.Pa libprivateprotobuf-lite .
.Sh CAVEATS
Only the C++ generator is built in; the upstream Java, Python, C#,
Objective-C, PHP, Ruby, Rust and Kotlin generators are not part of the base
system.
The C++ runtime libraries are private to the base system: generated C++
code built outside the base system should use a Protocol Buffers runtime
and compiler from ports, not
.Pa /usr/libexec/protoc .
